column2:
**A file system uses a binary tree where each directory node has at most two subdirectories:**

```c
struct Directory {
    char name[50];
    struct Directory *left_subdir;
    struct Directory *right_subdir;
};
```

**What property distinguishes a binary tree from other tree structures?**

**A startup's organizational structure is represented as a binary tree:**

```c
struct Employee {
    int emp_id;
    char name[50];
    struct Employee *left_report;
    struct Employee *right_report;
};

struct Employee* createEmployee(int id, char* name) {
    struct Employee* newEmp = malloc(sizeof(struct Employee));
    newEmp->emp_id = id;
    strcpy(newEmp->name, name);
    newEmp->left_report = NULL;
    newEmp->right_report = NULL;
    return newEmp;
}
```

**What is the significance of setting both pointers to NULL during node creation?**

**A customer service chatbot uses a binary tree for decision flow:**

```c
void processQuery(TreeNode* node) {
    if (node->left == NULL && node->right == NULL) {
        printf("Solution: %s\n", node->solution);
        return;
    }
    // Continue traversing based on user response
}
```

**What does the condition check identify?**

**A social media platform displays comment threads in preorder traversal:**

```c
void displayComments(Comment* root) {
    if (root == NULL) return;
    printf("Comment by %s: %s\n", root->author, root->text);
    displayComments(root->left);
    displayComments(root->right);
}
```

**Given a tree: Root(A) -> Left(B) -> Right(C), where B has children D(left) and E(right), what is the display order?**

**A music app analyzes song preferences using inorder traversal:**

```c
void analyzeSongs(SongNode* root) {
    if (root == NULL) return;
    analyzeSongs(root->left);
    printf("Song: %s - Plays: %d\n", root->title, root->play_count);
    analyzeSongs(root->right);
}
```

**For a BST storing songs sorted by play count, what advantage does inorder traversal provide?**

**A CDN network uses postorder traversal to shut down servers:**

```c
void shutdownServers(Server* root) {
    if (root == NULL) return;
    shutdownServers(root->left);
    shutdownServers(root->right);
    printf("Shutting down server: %s\n", root->name);
    freeServer(root);
}
```

**Why is postorder traversal appropriate for this deletion operation?**

**An emergency room uses level-order traversal to process patients:**

```c
void processPatients(PatientNode* root) {
    Queue* q = createQueue();
    enqueue(q, root);
    while (!isEmpty(q)) {
        PatientNode* current = dequeue(q);
        treatPatient(current);
        if (current->left) enqueue(q, current->left);
        if (current->right) enqueue(q, current->right);
    }
}
```

**What characteristic of level-order traversal makes it suitable for this triage scenario?**

**An online learning platform calculates total course duration:**

```c
int calculateTotalHours(Course* root) {
    if (root == NULL) return 0;
    return root->duration + 
           calculateTotalHours(root->left) + 
           calculateTotalHours(root->right);
}
```

**If the tree has courses: Root(10hrs), Left(5hrs), Right(8hrs), Left->Left(3hrs), what is the total?**

**A warehouse counts total inventory items:**

```c
int countItems(Warehouse* root) {
    if (root == NULL) return 0;
    return 1 + countItems(root->left) + countItems(root->right);
}
```

**For a complete binary tree of height 3, how many warehouse locations are counted?**

**A smart home system measures network depth:**

```c
int findMaxDepth(Device* root) {
    if (root == NULL) return 0;
    int leftDepth = findMaxDepth(root->left);
    int rightDepth = findMaxDepth(root->right);
    return 1 + (leftDepth > rightDepth ? leftDepth : rightDepth);
}
```

**What does this function calculate for the device network?**

**A cloud storage service mirrors folder structures:**

```c
Folder* mirrorStructure(Folder* root) {
    if (root == NULL) return NULL;
    Folder* newRoot = createFolder(root->name);
    newRoot->left = mirrorStructure(root->right);
    newRoot->right = mirrorStructure(root->left);
    return newRoot;
}
```

**What transformation does this function perform?**

**A game checks if two players have identical achievement trees:**

```c
bool compareAchievements(Achievement* tree1, Achievement* tree2) {
    if (tree1 == NULL && tree2 == NULL) return true;
    if (tree1 == NULL || tree2 == NULL) return false;
    return (tree1->id == tree2->id) &&
           compareAchievements(tree1->left, tree2->left) &&
           compareAchievements(tree1->right, tree2->right);
}
```

**What condition must be satisfied for the function to return true?**

**A restaurant app finds specific menu items:**

```c
MenuItem* findDish(MenuItem* root, int dish_id) {
    if (root == NULL || root->id == dish_id) return root;
    MenuItem* leftResult = findDish(root->left, dish_id);
    if (leftResult != NULL) return leftResult;
    return findDish(root->right, dish_id);
}
```

**What search strategy does this function implement?**

**A fitness app checks if goal tree is balanced:**

```c
bool isBalanced(Goal* root) {
    if (root == NULL) return true;
    int leftHeight = getHeight(root->left);
    int rightHeight = getHeight(root->right);
    if (abs(leftHeight - rightHeight) > 1) return false;
    return isBalanced(root->left) && isBalanced(root->right);
}
```

**What defines a balanced binary tree in this context?**

**A task scheduler finds the lowest common ancestor of two tasks:**

```c
Task* findLCA(Task* root, int task1, int task2) {
    if (root == NULL) return NULL;
    if (root->id == task1 || root->id == task2) return root;
    Task* leftLCA = findLCA(root->left, task1, task2);
    Task* rightLCA = findLCA(root->right, task1, task2);
    if (leftLCA && rightLCA) return root;
    return leftLCA ? leftLCA : rightLCA;
}
```

**What does the Lowest Common Ancestor represent in a task dependency tree?**

**A streaming service converts between tree representations:**

```c
void serializeTree(Video* root, FILE* file) {
    if (root == NULL) {
        fprintf(file, "NULL ");
        return;
    }
    fprintf(file, "%d ", root->video_id);
    serializeTree(root->left, file);
    serializeTree(root->right, file);
}
```

**What is the purpose of serialization in this video catalog system?**

**A blockchain validator sums all transaction values:**

```c
long long sumTransactions(Block* root) {
    if (root == NULL) return 0;
    return root->value + 
           sumTransactions(root->left) + 
           sumTransactions(root->right);
}
```

**For a tree with Root(100), Left(50), Right(75), Left->Left(25), Right->Right(30), what is the sum?**

**A social network finds users at a specific connection distance:**

```c
void findConnectionsAtLevel(User* root, int target_level, int current_level) {
    if (root == NULL) return;
    if (current_level == target_level) {
        printf("Suggested: %s\n", root->name);
        return;
    }
    findConnectionsAtLevel(root->left, target_level, current_level + 1);
    findConnectionsAtLevel(root->right, target_level, current_level + 1);
}
```

**What does this function accomplish in friend suggestion algorithm?**
